WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.102
-Congratulations on a sixth
season of "The Blacklist."

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-It's amazing.

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:04.437 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You've got Glenda Jackson
here tonight.

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:06.673 size:88% position:44%
-How exciting is that?
I mean, I'm very excited

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.508
you're here, don't get me wrong.
-Yeah.

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But Glenda Jackson, yeah.
I'm glad.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.045
-Because I want to see -- is she
going to talk about "King Lear"?

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.547
-Yes, she's playing King Lear.
-I know, I can't wait to see it.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You'll go see it, though?
-Yeah, of course.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:17.851 line:92%
I saw her in "Three Tall Women."

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.818 line:92%
-"Three Tall Women" was amazing.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you go to a lot
of Broadway shows?

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.423 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I try.
I mean, things are busy.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:24.491 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-Yeah. You're so busy,

00:00:24.491 --> 00:00:27.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you have time to even
watch the news?

00:00:27.494 --> 00:00:29.896 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Can you even do that?

00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:31.664 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't watch the news.
-Yeah.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:35.668
-I don't watch the news at all.
I read the news.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:40.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know,
I read it every day.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It comes out every day.
-Yeah.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:43.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.446 size:81% position:41%
But I -- I don't know,
I read a lot of news.

00:00:46.446 --> 00:00:49.249
You know, I don't know.
It goes in cycles for me.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:55.688
I'm having a terrible conundrum
now of how to process the news.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:56.389 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Today.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:57.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't think you're alone.
A lot of --

00:00:57.524 --> 00:01:02.395
-Right. And so, you know, so I
sometimes -- but I vacillate,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.764 line:92%
like, in all things in my life,

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:08.168 align:start size:94% position:6%
I have never figured out
moderation

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.070 line:92%
in any way, shape, or form.

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.639
And it's that way with the news
as well,

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:17.110
where it's either for me
just consuming a ton of it

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
and trying to figure out
a way to, you know,

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:23.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
put it together and process it
and get rid of it.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:28.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then that, or sometimes it
just has to be a blackout.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:29.823 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll skip the first section
of the paper,

00:01:29.823 --> 00:01:33.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll go right to, you know,
the later sections.

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you feel better
on those days?

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6%
-In some ways.
-Yeah.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.868
-I think that the certain things
in the news are being --

00:01:41.868 --> 00:01:43.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're seeing too much of it.
Especially --

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:46.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes I succumb to the
24-hour news cycle.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.974
-Yeah.
-Which, I'm very envious of you.

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:51.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because I was thinking about
this tonight.

00:01:51.311 --> 00:01:53.413
You know, I was actually talking
to the producer backstage

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:57.283 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the fact that you're
forced to process it.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you really --
-Yes.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:01:59.986 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:04.257 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And in a way,
it's tremendously digestive.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah.
-You can consume it,

00:02:05.558 --> 00:02:09.028
you can metabolize it,
and then you can [bleep] it out.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.165 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know what I mean?
And get rid of it.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:15.235
-Yeah. And I get to [bleep] it
out in front of an audience.

00:02:15.235 --> 00:02:17.203 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Right, right, right.

00:02:17.203 --> 00:02:19.205 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.508 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Fantastic. Anyway...

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:22.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to talk about
simpler times.

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:24.444 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because one of my favorite
things about when you

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:27.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
come on the show
is you have wonderful stories

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:28.081 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
about growing up.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:30.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I want to ask,
you took a lot of family trips

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:33.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
with your family,
as you do with family trips.

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:36.990
And I -- because I'm excited
about traveling with my kids.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.591 line:92%
Your family went to Europe.

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would drive around
in a VW, what, van?

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:42.829 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Van. Yeah.

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How is that?
-VW bus.

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.466 line:92%
-A VW bus. That's so Bohemian.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:48.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Vanagon was the first
VW van.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:51.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we didn't have a Vanagon.
I wanted a Vanagon.

00:02:51.371 --> 00:02:53.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just felt great.
There was a popup thing.

00:02:53.773 --> 00:02:55.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-There was, you know,

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:57.877
anything that had a fridge in it
seemed great.

00:02:57.877 --> 00:03:01.614 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But, you know, I...

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
yes, the VW bus
was our transport.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:08.254
My parents were teachers, and we
didn't really have much money.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:10.690 size:78% position:39%
You know, they didn't
earn very much money.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:14.093 size:78% position:39%
But what we did have
is every seven years,

00:03:14.093 --> 00:03:15.862 size:81% position:41% line:92%
they got a sabbatical,

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:20.934
which means that you get
a paid vacation, basically.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:24.103 size:88% position:44%
And they went to Europe
because we have cousins,

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
Italian cousins, and so
we'd go over to --

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:29.008 size:84% position:42%
For the two sabbaticals
when I was growing up,

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.511 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there were, we went over
to Europe both times.

00:03:31.511 --> 00:03:35.682
And both times we picked up a --
we got a van --

00:03:35.682 --> 00:03:38.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
a Volkswagen bus,
and we drove around Europe,

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then the Volkswagen bus
became our car

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
back in the States.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was such a hit that
you got one in the states?

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:47.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, that car
became -- that bus

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.997
became our car
in the United States both times.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:54.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You brought it back?
-It was a trip to Europe,

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the car buying --
you know, we drove around --

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:59.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You went to Europe to buy
your car?

00:03:59.572 --> 00:04:00.640 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-To drive around Europe.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, no,
I understand that part.

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:02.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's the normal part.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then it would
come back with us.

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.178 line:92%
-That's not the normal part.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:06.346 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Then it would
come back with us.

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
-And it was great

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:10.116 align:start size:94% position:6%
because for me, these are
the --

00:04:10.116 --> 00:04:12.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was in the days
sort of before seat belts.

00:04:12.452 --> 00:04:16.889
I mean, the '50s. I wasn't born
when the seat belts started.

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:18.191 size:75% position:38% line:92%
But it was before --

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was still when you're
ignoring seat belts.

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:20.893 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.763
They had them, but nobody
thought they mattered.

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.331
-Yeah. They were something
that you sort of like --

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.967
You're sitting on something,
you want to get rid of it.

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:31.070 size:84% position:42%
But I never experienced
a seat belt, really,

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
because my domain was
the wayback.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:35.775
You know the wayback?
The wayback. That's what I had.

00:04:35.775 --> 00:04:36.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Which, I think

00:04:36.609 --> 00:04:38.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's changed now.
-Okay, the wayback,

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
meaning just the way back
of the van?

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:42.181
-Yeah, it's where the suitcases
and kids go.

00:04:42.181 --> 00:04:44.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-And you're just like --

00:04:44.284 --> 00:04:46.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
And at that point, because you
didn't have to be seated,

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:49.522 size:78% position:39%
belted into anything.
There weren't seats.

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
The wayback was just a space
for luggage, you know?

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:54.193 line:92%
And you would go back in there.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:56.296 size:81% position:41%
-So you would just sit
amongst the luggage?

00:04:56.296 --> 00:05:00.533
-Yeah, I'd be -- if you're in
the wayback, you take a pillow.

00:05:00.533 --> 00:05:01.901 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, so you'd have

00:05:01.901 --> 00:05:04.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
a pillow back there.
And a bunch of suitcases

00:05:04.037 --> 00:05:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
up -- and you know,
it's, like, a space

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:08.574
a little bit smaller than this.
-Yeah.

00:05:08.574 --> 00:05:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you know,
you're sort of, like...

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You got a pillow.

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
That doesn't look that bad.

00:05:15.081 --> 00:05:17.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, I mean, it's
fantastic when you're a kid.

00:05:17.784 --> 00:05:20.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-So that couch is

00:05:20.253 --> 00:05:21.688 line:92%
the same sort of ratio --

00:05:21.688 --> 00:05:25.091
-I feel like you're trying
to sell me a van right now.

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-I am.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:29.896 line:92%
Vans are a great fantasy.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
I could have lived
in the wayback.

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yes.
Anyway, that was --

00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:39.806
and also that became the last VW
bus that we drove around Europe

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:44.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then came back and brought
it back with us.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
That became my first car.
-Really?

00:05:45.778 --> 00:05:50.450
-Yeah. And it was fantastic
because I went to this school

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:51.150 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in Massachusetts.

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
It was a big, huge, sort of
college-sized boarding school,

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:59.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was a day student.
I lived in the next town over.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:03.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I had a Volkswagen bus.
It was crazy, you know?

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:07.033
-I mean, you were like
the towny kid with a bus?

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:07.667 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-With a bus, yeah.

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.303
-I mean, you must have been
the coolest kid at that school.

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.871 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Well...

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:17.610
We'll talk about that next time.
James Spader, everybody!

